      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few ways to phrase that, keeping it professional and focused on solutions. You can start by saying, \"I've been tracking the scope of the new project, and it's growing larger than our current team capacity can comfortably handle.\" Then, you can suggest the options: \"To ensure we deliver the high-quality results you expect, we need to either allocate additional resources or adjust the timeline.\" This frames it as a logistical challenge, not a complaint.\n\n*If you want a slightly softer approach, you could say:* \"As we dive deeper into the project, it's become clear that the scope is quite substantial. To maintain our standards, I wanted to bring up the possibility of either bringing on some extra support or revisiting the delivery date.\"\n\nRemember to always end by reaffirming your commitment to the project's success! Good luck with the email.",
